  "description": "s013 step 2 (q-Bessel gate). (A) DERIVES the colored Lawrence-Rozansky residue character of Sigma(2,3,5) exactly: 2sinh(z/2)2sinh(z/3)2sinh(alpha z/5)/2sinh(z) = num_alpha(x)*Sum_{k>=0} x^{60k} (x=e^{-z/30}), sympy-exact + 50dps verification, folded into an odd 60-periodic character with per-class consistency votes; alpha=1 reproduces the bare {1,11,19,29} support; ALL residue weights are +-1 (pure sign, no magnitude) -- the value map cannot live in the residue data. (B) Decomposes the colored family into the 8 per-exponent false-theta channels Psi~^(e)(1/q0); the alpha=1 channel sum reproduces the bare invariant 2.3296 (validation). (C) Screens channels/pair-sums/pair-diffs against the d_q targets and verifies the analytic q->1 gate: channel ratios -> L(0,chi_e) proportional to (30-e), DECREASING in e while d_q INCREASES -- the channel amplitude is refuted at every anchor. (D) Gates the single-argument (q-)Bessel vacuum row (ordinary J_e(x) vs classical dims 1,4,5,6; Hahn-Exton J_e(x;1/q0^2) vs d_q; plus pair-symmetrized variants) with the 1-dof overdetermined test (pin x on the first ratio, 2 net cross-checks at every root). Scope (a) prunes only; the genuine E_q(2) q-Hankel/Plancherel kernel remains the open step (primary literature firewalled: arXiv 403 in sandbox). No fit; nothing wired.",
